course: dictionary
lesson: 16120
title: Old-fashioned words
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Some words are old-fashioned. People stopped using them long ago, but you still meet them in old books, plays and poems. «Wherefore» is one of these words. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they give you clues.
explain: «Wherefore» usually means «why». In Shakespeare's play, Juliet asks, «Wherefore art thou Romeo?», which means «Why are you Romeo?» She is not asking where he is. The clues help: she is upset that Romeo belongs to an enemy family.
explain: Today you will mostly hear «wherefore» in one phrase, «the whys and wherefores». It means all the reasons and details behind something. To check a new meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Wherefore» is old-fashioned, so you will mostly find it in old books, plays and poems.
fact: «Wherefore» means why, or for what reason.
fact: «Wherefore» can also mean therefore, which means for that reason.
fact: «The whys and wherefores» means all the reasons and details behind something.
fact: Do not mistake «wherefore» for «where». In Shakespeare it means why.
exercise: «Wherefore did you leave the party so early?» What does wherefore mean here? | *Why | When | Who | Where
exercise: «He was tired, wherefore he went to bed early.» What does wherefore mean here? | Slowly | Who | Where | *Therefore, for that reason
exercise: The teacher explained the whys and wherefores of the new rule. What does whys and wherefores mean? | Long, boring stories | The places where things happen | *All the reasons and details | Very old rules
test: In Juliet's line «Wherefore art thou Romeo?», what does wherefore mean? | Where | How | Who | *Why
test: «The bridge was closed, wherefore we took the long road home.» What does wherefore mean here? | Quickly | *Therefore, for that reason | Where | Who
exam: Jayden reads «Wherefore, I ask, did the king leave the room?» What does wherefore mean? | Who | *Why | Where | When
